--
N5008 [expr.new]/1 + [temp.variadic]/5: a new-initializer's expression-list
is a pack-expansion context, and [temp.param]/14: a function template's
parameter pack need not be its last template parameter.  libc++'s
`template <class T, class... Args, class = decltype(::new(declval<void *>())
T(declval<Args>()...))> construct_at(T *, Args &&...)' called with NO
arguments (basic_string::__begin_lifetime) failed twice: the empty pack in
the constraint's new-initializer was not expanded before type-checking (no
viable candidate), and the instantiation-time empty-pack strip only looked
at a TRAILING pack, leaving `static_cast<Args &&>(args)...' in the body
("symbol 'args' is unknown").
